    "quick_recipe": "So I looked it up and a bunch of recipes use old English cheese which is shelf stable but expensive. Then I saw recipes using velveeta so I used that.\nWas 1 block of velveeta to 1 pound of sausage for one pack of English muffins.\nCook the sausage till it's almost done in a pan all chopped up obviously, then in the velveeta all blocked up and melt it all together and put on the muffins.\nThen 10 minutes in the oven at 350.",
    "has_quick_recipe": true,
    "note": null
  },
  {
    "title": "Baked Beans w/ Cheese Bake",
    "external_links": [],
    "google_doc_links": [
      {
        "text": "Quick_Recipe",
        "url": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CuMAKzifKbd6_c60qiHlBijP32Ol3vW2/edit"
      }
    ],
    "picture_links": [],
    "quick_recipe": "Ingredients:\n1 pound ground beef\n1 small onion – chopped.\n16 ounce can baked beans (I use Bush’s Original)\n1 green pepper – chopped.\n½ cup BBQ sauce\n1-2 cups shredded cheddar cheese.\nInstructions:\nBrown ground beef, green pepper, and onion together. Drain grease.\nMix with baked beans and BBQ sauce.\nPour in casserole dish.\nBake at 350 degrees for 35 minutes.\nPut shredded cheese on top and return to oven just long enough to melt the cheese.",
    "has_quick_recipe": true,
    "note": null
